---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import '../styles/globals.css';

const sections = [
  {
    href: '/ubiquitous-language/',
    title: 'Ubiquitous Language',
    description:
      'The vocabulary of the Account domain. Concepts, relationships, and the consolidated model.',
    meta: '7 chapters',
  },
  {
    href: '/formal-laws/',
    title: 'Formal Laws',
    description:
      'The invariants D1–D6 that any implementation must preserve. Each law set is self-contained.',
    meta: '6 law sets',
  },
  {
    href: '/architecture/',
    title: 'Architecture',
    description:
      'Interactive C4 diagrams rendered from the workspace model.',
    meta: 'C4',
  },
];
---

<DocLayout title="Sovereign Account">
  <div class="max-w-3xl">
    <header class="mb-10 sm:mb-14">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-primary leading-tight">
        Sovereign Account
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 sm:mt-5 text-lg sm:text-xl text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        A universal primitive for sovereign identity, authority, and execution.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="mb-10 sm:mb-14">
      <p class="text-text leading-relaxed">
        Sovereign Account defines a formal model that lets an application determine:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 pl-5 list-disc text-text-muted leading-relaxed marker:text-primary">
        <li>Which sovereign <code class="text-text">Identity</code> is exercising authority.</li>
        <li>What authority exists for that identity.</li>
        <li>Which subject or mechanism may exercise that authority.</li>
        <li>Under what conditions it may be exercised.</li>
        <li>Which action the consuming context requests.</li>
        <li>Whether that exercise is authorized.</li>
        <li>How an authorized decision is materialized.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        The domain is implementation-agnostic. It does not depend on a specific
        blockchain, virtual machine, cryptographic curve, or account-abstraction
        standard.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10 sm:mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 sm:mb-6">Explore</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-4 grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {sections.map((s) => (
          <a
            href={s.href}
            class="group flex flex-col rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface-raised p-4 sm:p-5 transition-colors hover:border-primary"
          >
            <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-1">
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-base sm:text-lg group-hover:text-primary transition-colors">
                {s.title}
              </h3>
              <span class="text-xs text-text-muted whitespace-nowrap pt-1">
                {s.meta}
              </span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
              {s.description}
            </p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="border-t border-border pt-6">
      <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        Made with 💚 —{' '}
        <a
          href="https://github.com/AndresChanchi/sovereign-account"
          class="text-primary hover:underline"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          view source on GitHub →
        </a>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</DocLayout>
